var ITEMS=[["What plumbers do","Plumbers install and repair the pipes, fixtures, and systems that bring clean water in and take waste out. It is a licensed trade in most places, learned through 4-5 year apprenticeships combining paid work with classroo"], ["Essential tools","Two pipe wrenches (one to hold, one to turn), adjustable wrench, tubing cutter, plunger, drain snake, basin wrench, Teflon tape, plumber's putty, torch and solder for copper, and a bright flashlight. Pros add: press-fit "], ["Key skills","Reading blueprints and isometric drawings, soldering copper, solvent-welding PVC/ABS/CPVC, threading steel pipe, diagnosing pressure and drainage problems, and sequencing rough-in before finish work. Plus: clear communic"], ["Safety essentials","Know the main water shutoff before starting any job. Eye protection for soldering and cutting; ventilate solvents and flux; never test for gas with a flame; lift with your legs \u2014 cast iron and water heaters are brutal."], ["Getting started","Finish high school (math helps), find a union or non-union apprenticeship, get an apprentice license, log roughly 8,000 hours over 4-5 years, then pass the journeyman exam. Many start as helpers to learn the ropes."], ["Pro tips","Photograph everything before disassembly. Keep an organizer of common washers, O-rings, and cartridges. Quote flat-rate for routine jobs. Always test at full pressure before leaving \u2014 and leave the space cleaner than you"], ["P-trap","Trade term \u2014 P-trap: The U-shaped pipe under sinks that holds water to block sewer gas."], ["DWV","Trade term \u2014 DWV: Drain-waste-vent: the gravity drainage system of a building."], ["Vent stack","Trade term \u2014 Vent stack: The pipe through the roof that lets drains breathe and traps hold water."], ["Cleanout","Trade term \u2014 Cleanout: An access cap in the drain line for clearing clogs."], ["Angle stop","Trade term \u2014 Angle stop: The small shutoff valve under sinks and toilets."], ["Flapper","Trade term \u2014 Flapper: The rubber seal in the toilet tank that lifts to flush."], ["Fill valve","Trade term \u2014 Fill valve: The toilet tank mechanism that refills water after a flush."], ["Wax ring","Trade term \u2014 Wax ring: The wax seal between a toilet and the floor flange."], ["Escutcheon","Trade term \u2014 Escutcheon: The decorative cover plate around a pipe at the wall."], ["Dielectric union","Trade term \u2014 Dielectric union: A fitting that joins copper to steel without galvanic corrosion."], ["Sweat fitting","Trade term \u2014 Sweat fitting: A copper joint sealed with solder and heat."], ["Compression fitting","Trade term \u2014 Compression fitting: A joint sealed by compressing a ferrule ring onto the pipe."], ["Push-fit fitting","Trade term \u2014 Push-fit fitting: A fitting that grips pipe with internal teeth and O-rings; no tools needed."], ["PEX","Trade term \u2014 PEX: Flexible cross-linked polyethylene tubing, the modern repipe standard."], ["Flux","Trade term \u2014 Flux: The paste that cleans copper so solder flows into the joint."], ["Anode rod","Trade term \u2014 Anode rod: The sacrificial rod inside water heaters that prevents tank rust."], ["T&P valve","Trade term \u2014 T&P valve: Temperature and pressure relief valve on water heaters; a critical safety device."], ["Water hammer arrestor","Trade term \u2014 Water hammer arrestor: A cushion device that stops banging pipes."], ["Backflow preventer","Trade term \u2014 Backflow preventer: A device that keeps contaminated water from flowing back into clean supply."]];
